WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.720
High school is a turbulent time for a lot of&nbsp;
us, to say the least. Subjects are a lot harder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.760
classes feel longer, and because you’re older&nbsp;
there can be so much more pressure put on you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.800
by your teachers and parents alike. There’s&nbsp;
a lot more onus for you to perform well in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.240
tests and make sure that you get high grades,&nbsp;
thanks to everyone around you telling you that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:27.200
these are ‘the most important years of your&nbsp;
life’ or that your high school experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.640
will ‘determine your whole future for good&nbsp;
or bad’. Actually, come to think of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.840
‘pressure’ feels like a bit of an understatement.
As if there weren’t already enough things to worry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.000
about when you’re trying to make your way&nbsp;
through high school, the changes to yourself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.440
get thrown into the mix as well. Growing up and&nbsp;
getting older often means developing a further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:53.840
previously unseen level of self-awareness&nbsp;
and understanding of who you are as a person;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.680
that can be true of any part of life, but high&nbsp;
school can often be the first time we’re aware&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.320
of ourselves in such a heightened way.
Usually, everything we’re experiencing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.960
during that time can make some of us&nbsp;
self-conscious, shying away from others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:14.000
to avoid embarrassment or becoming brash&nbsp;
and loud to over-compensate for just how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.200
uncertain they might be feeling deep down.
Then, of course, on top of that already huge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.960
mountain, romantic feelings get thrown into the&nbsp;
mix as well. Sure, in the grand scheme of things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.840
high school romances are usually just tiny,&nbsp;
almost insignificant footnotes in the stories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:35.440
of our lives. But obviously, they don’t feel&nbsp;
like it at the time. When you’re right there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.440
living through that part of your life without&nbsp;
the benefit of hindsight that comes later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:44.400
your high school crush can feel like&nbsp;
the very center of the entire universe.&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.520
Being introduced to and surrounded by more&nbsp;
people than ever, more than any previous stage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:54.880
of schooling, means that romantic feelings usually&nbsp;
have a higher likelihood of developing, and are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:00.000
made more prominent by the whole other whirlwind&nbsp;
of things that high school brings with it.&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.480
Case in point, Elly was having this exact problem.&nbsp;
For as long as she could remember, she had never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:12.480
really got people. They were confusing,&nbsp;
complicated, and completely unpredictable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.600
Usually, they frustrated Elly, which made it&nbsp;
hard for her to talk to most of her classmates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.400
especially if she didn’t already know them that&nbsp;
well. The common ground could sometimes make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:28.080
it a little easier, it helped break the ice, but&nbsp;
finding those shared interests or similarities was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:35.760
often harder than just spending time on her own.
Then, along came Markus, or ‘Marky’ as Elly heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:41.360
he preferred to be called. On the first day of the&nbsp;
semester, she had been placed in a new math class.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.760
The second Marky came walking through&nbsp;
the door, she immediately found herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:51.280
unable to keep her eyes off him; especially&nbsp;
because he ended up taking the seat directly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:57.040
in front of hers, meaning he was always filling up&nbsp;
most of her view when she looked straight ahead.&nbsp;

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:02.560
Despite looking like a skater type, from what&nbsp;
Elly observed, Marky was pretty sharp. She was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:07.440
no slouch herself, usually noting down correct&nbsp;
answers a few moments before whoever the teacher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:13.680
called on. Whenever Marky was called on, he also&nbsp;
had the exact right solution to whatever problem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.240
or equation the rest of the class was probably&nbsp;
still struggling to keep up with. Despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:24.080
knowing very little about him, Elly couldn’t help&nbsp;
feeling a certain new and unfamiliar way towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:30.160
this particular classmate. It was like they were&nbsp;
both operating at the same speed, on identical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:35.680
wavelengths, if only she knew more about him.
And it was during class that Elly had an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.760
idea about how she could get to know&nbsp;
him better, but without the awkward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.200
uncomfortable interactions that came from&nbsp;
slipping about on the ice rather than breaking it.&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:51.360
She could use the doll. Sure, she had been mulling&nbsp;
it over, toying with the possibility for a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.360
but wasn’t certain that it was right&nbsp;
for her to follow that course of action.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:00.880
But as the days turned into weeks, getting deeper&nbsp;
and deeper into the semester brought with it the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:06.800
possibility that another girl would catch Marky’s&nbsp;
attention the way he’d caught Elly’s. Just the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:12.400
thought of that alone made her want to cry,&nbsp;
she couldn’t bear to see it become a reality.&nbsp;

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:18.240
One day in class, her chance presented&nbsp;
itself, on what had been an unusually hot day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:22.560
The scorching heat outdoors was causing&nbsp;
all the students to groan in discomfort,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.200
barely able to acknowledge anything other&nbsp;
than the high temperature. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:32.560
all the teachers could possibly do was open up&nbsp;
the windows to counteract the relentless weather,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.680
but it was nothing more than a futile gesture.
Sitting down in front of Elly, Marky shrugged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:42.800
off the denim jacket he always wore, leaving&nbsp;
it hanging over the back of his chair. Her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:49.120
eyes honed in on what she needed. Clinging to the&nbsp;
surface of the acid-washed material was a single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:55.040
strand of black hair. She knew she had to pick her&nbsp;
moment carefully. If the teacher, or any of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.040 --> 00:05:00.560
other students in the class – or, worst of all,&nbsp;
Marky himself – saw what she was doing, it would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:07.200
look beyond weird. Leaning forward on her desk as&nbsp;
subtly as she could, Elly slowly reached forward.&nbsp;

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.920
Her fingers wouldn’t reach, the back of Marky’s&nbsp;
chair was just an inch or two further than her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:17.600
arms extended. Elly felt her heart stop for a&nbsp;
split second as her crush moved in his chair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:21.520
the shift causing the jacket to move&nbsp;
and the strand of his hair dropped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.720
almost falling out of sight. Sighing with relief&nbsp;
as silently as she could, when she saw the black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:33.280
streak managed to stay attached to the denim,&nbsp;
Elly fished a pen out from inside her pencil case.&nbsp;

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:37.520
Leaning forward again, she delicately&nbsp;
lifted the pointed tip of her pen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:42.720
hooking the hair on it. Pulling it back towards&nbsp;
her before anyone saw, she covered it with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:48.320
hand, both to hide what she had done and to stop&nbsp;
the precious hair from being caught by the warm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:53.760
humid breeze pouring through the open windows.
Gently, Elly placed the one missing component she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:58.880
needed into a clean tissue, which she then&nbsp;
folded four times and kept in her jacket,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:03.600
constantly checking throughout the day to make&nbsp;
sure it was still there. On more than one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:08.400
those quick spot checks, Elly felt her heart&nbsp;
plummet downwards for a second when she couldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:13.920
immediately feel the tissue in her pocket, only to&nbsp;
calm down a second later to realize it was still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:20.720
there, with its precious contents too. The rest&nbsp;
of the day she felt tense, drumming her fingers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:26.800
together in impatience, every hour feeling like&nbsp;
it would go on forever. It was just a case of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:33.920
waiting out the day, until that final bell rung.
The moment she was able, she rushed away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:38.800
the school, walking home as quickly as she&nbsp;
possibly could, one hand in her pocket to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:44.720
keep the hair secure. Elly was lucky enough –&nbsp;
or unlucky depending on your view – to live in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:49.840
the same town as her school, and not too&nbsp;
far away to need the bus. She could make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:54.400
her way there on foot in pretty decent time.
Normally, the busses from the school would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.400 --> 00:07:00.160
pass her as she walked. Looking up, she saw one of&nbsp;
the huge yellow vehicles driving down the street,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:05.920
and a familiar face sat at a window seat:&nbsp;
Marky. Seeing him, Elly quickened her pace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:10.400
speed-walking home. The moment she unlocked&nbsp;
the front door and closed it behind her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:16.160
she threw off her backpack and raced upstairs to&nbsp;
her bedroom. She knew exactly where she’d left it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:22.400
As she flipped on her lamp, it was laying there&nbsp;
on the desk ready for her: the Knotty Stalker.&nbsp;

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:27.760
The tiny doll was made of one single knitted&nbsp;
string, with a pair of shiny onyx beads against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:33.040
the red of its face, in the place of eyes. Elly&nbsp;
had come across the little oddity in a box of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:37.760
her grandmother’s things. Although she never&nbsp;
knew her all that well, after she had died,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:43.360
Elly’s mom had gone to clear her house up, and&nbsp;
came back with a few boxes full of keepsakes.&nbsp;

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:47.200
“These are all your grandma’s things I&nbsp;
couldn’t sell, or think of what to do with,”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:52.240
her mother explained, offering her the cardboard&nbsp;
box. “If you can pick out anything that you like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:57.600
it’s yours, El. I’m sure grandma won’t mind.”
Looking inside, there wasn’t much save for a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:02.800
old clothes, knick-knacks, souvenirs, and trinkets&nbsp;
that were mostly all broken, or the odd piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:08.160
of jewelry that looked too worn out and rusted&nbsp;
to wear. But right at the bottom was the doll.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:12.720
It was wrapped up in a crumpled piece of paper&nbsp;
that might have been clear white at some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:18.800
but had changed shades with age. Unfolding it,&nbsp;
Elly read the message inscribed on one side:&nbsp;

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.600
“Congratulations on your purchase of a&nbsp;
genuine Knotty Stalker! Do you love someone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.600
but they won't give you the time of day? Do&nbsp;
you wish you could hear what they say about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:33.120
you behind their back? Well, wonder no more!&nbsp;
Using this fantabulous product, you can keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:39.040
track of your loved ones' every move, their every&nbsp;
word! All you have to do is get a single hair from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:44.400
the head of the object of your desires, slip&nbsp;
it under a loose string on our Knotty Stalker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:50.480
and see what you're missing! Another wonderful&nbsp;
product brought to you by The Factory.”&nbsp;

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:55.920
Now, that same crumpled note was in Elly’s hands;&nbsp;
her eyes scanning over the instructions a final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.920 --> 00:09:01.360
time to make sure she knew exactly what to do.&nbsp;
She didn’t much care for the name of it though;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:07.120
‘Knotty Stalker’, the latter word had a very&nbsp;
negative connotation. What she was doing here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:12.720
wasn’t stalking, Elly told herself, she just&nbsp;
wanted an easier way to learn about Marky. Surely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.400
there wasn’t anything wrong with that
Pulling the tissue from her pocket,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:21.840
she carefully lay it flat on the desk and unfolded&nbsp;
it. The hair was still there, secured between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:27.280
the thin folded paper. Delicately holding it&nbsp;
between her finger and thumb, Elly held the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:33.040
dark strand of Marky’s hair in the light of her&nbsp;
desk lamp. She treated it as gently as she could,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:38.160
making sure not to break the hair, worried&nbsp;
that the doll might not work if it snapped.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.960
Taking great care, she slipped it through one&nbsp;
of the loops in the Knotty Stalker’s string.&nbsp;

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:47.600
For a moment, nothing happened, the doll just&nbsp;
lay there on the wooden surface of the desk.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:52.720
It was completely still, not showing&nbsp;
even the slightest hint of any change.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.120
Feeling the worry building more and more, her&nbsp;
heart drumming against her chest so loud that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:02.160
she could practically hear it, Elly started&nbsp;
frantically looking back over the instructions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:07.600
in case she had somehow missed a step. She had no&nbsp;
idea what was meant to happen, or even what she’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:12.240
been expecting, but she was starting to think&nbsp;
that this doll might just be an oddity from an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:18.160
old toy store that marketed them to children by&nbsp;
promising things that weren’t actually possible.&nbsp;

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:24.160
“See you later guys!” a tiny voice came from the&nbsp;
desk, causing Elly’s heart to lurch in shock.&nbsp;

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:28.320
The doll was standing upright on the&nbsp;
wooden surface; only seconds before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:34.640
it had been lying flat on its back. As if by its&nbsp;
own accord, the little knitted figure was upright,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:40.160
like it was a living thing. And it wasn’t just&nbsp;
standing, its arm was waving, and its chest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:45.600
was even gently undulating to mimic the motion&nbsp;
of breathing. The Knotty Stalker kept waving a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:51.520
moment, only to drop its head forward and make&nbsp;
an exhaling motion that seemed to be a sigh.&nbsp;

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:55.680
“I really wish they wouldn’t keep calling&nbsp;
me Marky,” the same voice spoke up again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.680 --> 00:11:00.880
this time more clearly coming from the doll.
Elly watched it closer, transfixed with utter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:06.080
fascination. She was aware of the concept of a&nbsp;
voodoo doll, a mystical charm that contained a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:11.120
person’s hair affixed to a crude figure in&nbsp;
order to influence them through magic. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:16.400
doll seemed much the same, except it was&nbsp;
mimicking Marky’s – Markus’ – every move.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:20.960
Elly had overheard him talking to some of&nbsp;
his friends in the corridors at school once,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.480
talking about home.
He lived in the next town over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:29.680
and the bus must have only just arrived there&nbsp;
because now the doll was walking on the spot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:35.360
the same heavy-limbed, tired walk home after a&nbsp;
long, strenuous day at school. She recognized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:40.080
the walk; it was the same one she did when&nbsp;
she made her own way back to her mom’s house.&nbsp;

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:43.760
For the rest of the night, Elly didn’t&nbsp;
take her eyes off the Knotty Stalker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:50.000
watching as it streamed Markus’ actions to her&nbsp;
live. She watched in real-time as he arrived home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:54.640
sat and did his homework, and went back&nbsp;
downstairs to eat dinner; all the while Elly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:59.600
was neglecting to do those same things herself.
At one point in the night, the doll started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:05.760
dancing around, singing into something invisible&nbsp;
in its hand. It made Elly smile uncontrollably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.680
to watch, she had figured out that Markus&nbsp;
was now playing some music through a pair of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:15.840
headphones or a speaker, and singing along into&nbsp;
a hairbrush, dancing like no one was watching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:21.200
the kind of thing that almost everyone does&nbsp;
when they’re alone but never admits to.&nbsp;

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:25.520
Turning to her computer, keeping one eye on&nbsp;
the doll, refusing to stop watching it even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:30.800
in her peripheral vision, Elly typed the lyrics&nbsp;
it was singing into a search engine. Immediately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:35.600
pages worth of results came up for the song and&nbsp;
the band that had sung it; they weren’t a group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:41.760
that she’d ever heard of or listened to before,&nbsp;
but it was Friday. She had all weekend. Using her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:46.720
mom’s bank card, Elly ordered herself a t-shirt&nbsp;
with the band’s name on it, premium delivery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:51.360
meant it would be there before school next week.
On Monday, she showed up at school wearing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:56.080
new shirt. It was a few sizes too big, but that&nbsp;
meant that the band’s logo printed on the front&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.080 --> 00:13:01.280
was bigger, and harder to miss. Elly had spent&nbsp;
almost her whole weekend watching the doll as it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:06.160
mimicked Markus’ movements. He hadn’t done much&nbsp;
but play video games and go to the skatepark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:11.840
but she made sure she knew what he was doing.&nbsp;
Any time she wasn’t watching, she was listening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:17.200
to the music he liked, getting familiar with it&nbsp;
to prepare herself for what was about to happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:22.560
as if she had been studying to get ready for a&nbsp;
test. Somehow, striding through the corridors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:28.720
full of students milling about first thing in&nbsp;
the morning, Elly felt more confident than ever.&nbsp;

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:33.200
“Hey, Markus,” she greeted, spotting her&nbsp;
crush rummaging around in his locker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.600
and walking straight up to him.
“Hey, uh,” he paused, looking over at her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:44.240
for what felt like the first time. “You’re,&nbsp;
um… sorry, we have class together right?”&nbsp;

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:48.240
“Math, yeah!” she replied, surprising&nbsp;
herself at how quickly she’d recovered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:53.040
from the blow that he didn’t know her&nbsp;
name. “I’m Elly, I sit right behind you.”&nbsp;

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:57.520
“Right, right!” Markus smiled, “You&nbsp;
don’t have to use my full name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:01.200
everyone just calls me ‘Marky’ around here.”
“But you don’t like that nickname,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:06.560
I can tell,” Elly shot him a smile, trying&nbsp;
to play do her best ‘mysterious’ voice.&nbsp;

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:10.400
“How can you tell?” he asked.
“Don’t tell anyone,” she leaned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:14.880
forward and whispered, “But I’m kinda psychic.”
They both laughed, and Elly caught Markus’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:19.280
eyes reading the band name on her shirt.
“Hey, I had no idea you were a Parallel Lunatics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:23.920
fan,” he remarked. “That’s my favorite band!”
“Well, I just started listening to them,”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:27.360
Elly replied. “Maybe you could&nbsp;
recommend me some more of their albums?”&nbsp;

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:32.000
Suddenly, the school bell sounded, interrupting&nbsp;
their conversation with the reminder that the day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:36.640
had to start. Waving goodbye and heading to&nbsp;
class, Elly was unable to stop herself from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:42.400
smiling now that her way in had worked. For the&nbsp;
rest of the week, she kept relying on the doll;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:45.600
every moment she wasn’t in class,&nbsp;
she was holding it to her ear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:51.360
listening to Markus’ half of every conversation.&nbsp;
The more she did, the more she learned about him;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:56.160
what music he liked, where he was thinking of&nbsp;
going to college, and what he wanted to study&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.160 --> 00:15:01.120
there. Every time she passed him in the hallway,&nbsp;
she’d give him a smile and a wave, just to remind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:07.120
him that she was there. It was a long game,&nbsp;
but she hoped it would end the way she wanted.&nbsp;

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:11.520
Nine days had passed since she had started using&nbsp;
the doll, and that’s when it started to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:16.560
somewhat unreliable. Over the weekend, it had&nbsp;
been moving as though Markus was at the skatepark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:21.600
again. But when Elly approached him to ask how&nbsp;
his weekend was and if he’d enjoyed going skating,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:26.560
he looked at her with confusion. Markus said he’d&nbsp;
been visiting his dad that weekend and didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:32.160
have time to go anywhere near the skatepark.
But that one inaccuracy was nothing compared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:37.840
to what she heard the doll say next. Still&nbsp;
using it to listen in on Markus’ conversations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:43.600
the Knotty Stalker had started relaying words that&nbsp;
made her heart shatter into a thousand fragments.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:49.280
She overheard him talking to a friend&nbsp;
about her, saying horrible things like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:53.760
how he thought she was weird and that she had&nbsp;
clearly listened to Parallel Lunatics just to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:58.880
get his attention. Worst of all was when&nbsp;
Elly heard Markus say, through the doll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:04.160
that he would never want to date a girl like her.
She was heartbroken, tears streaming down her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:09.920
face as she hid in a toilet cubicle during lunch&nbsp;
break. Sniffling, wiping her eyes in her baggy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:16.640
band t-shirt, Elly felt her sadness turning into&nbsp;
a wave of rising anger. Throwing the door open,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:20.480
she marched out of the bathroom and&nbsp;
started searching the school for Markus.&nbsp;

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:24.400
“How could you say those things about me?” she&nbsp;
yelled furiously when she found him sitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:28.560
on a window ledge halfway up a stairwell.
“Huh?” he mumbled, lifting up his headphones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:32.400
instantly noticing that she seemed&nbsp;
upset. “Hey, Elly, are you okay?”&nbsp;

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:36.080
“You’re a jerk!” she screamed, almost&nbsp;
choking on sobs that threatened to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:40.160
come bursting out in floods of tears. “Why&nbsp;
were you saying horrible stuff about me?”&nbsp;

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:45.200
“What are you talking about?” Markus&nbsp;
asked, his face looking utterly confused.&nbsp;

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:48.720
“Don’t play dumb! You said you thought I was&nbsp;
weird, that you’d never date someone like me!”&nbsp;

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:53.280
“Whoa, Elly, I don’t know who told&nbsp;
you that, but that’s not true!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:57.840
I mean, I don’t know you all that well, but I’d&nbsp;
never say anything like-” he tried to reply.&nbsp;

00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:03.360
“Liar!” she cut him off with another yell.&nbsp;
“I heard you, I was listening to every word!”&nbsp;

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:07.760
“What do you mean you were listening?” the&nbsp;
confusion on Markus’ face quickly turned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:12.400
concern; in his mind, he was quickly putting two&nbsp;
and two together, the band shirt, the questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:17.440
about the skatepark. “Have you been following me?”
Instantly, Elly felt her stomach flip, her anger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:22.080
partly dissipating and replaced with fear.
“No, no, it’s not like that!” she said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:26.960
trying to ease his look of obvious alarm. “I just&nbsp;
wanted to know more about you, and now I do!”&nbsp;

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:31.920
“What the hell does that mean?” Markus&nbsp;
asked, sounding almost frightened.&nbsp;

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:37.360
“I know everything about you,” Elly started&nbsp;
stepping closer, thinking if she went in for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:42.640
hug that it might calm them both down. “I know all&nbsp;
your favorite music, what you like to do for fun.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:46.160
I wanted to know because I really like&nbsp;
you, but I didn’t know how to talk to you.”&nbsp;

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.960
“Stay away from me!”
Instinctively, Markus’ arms reacted to her getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:56.400
too close, pushing Elly backward. Behind her was&nbsp;
nothing but a sharp drop and a flight of concrete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.400 --> 00:18:01.440
steps. With a scream, she tumbled backward, her&nbsp;
body barrelling down the stairs until her head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:07.200
hit the ground at the bottom of the last one,&nbsp;
giving a sickening crack as her neck broke.&nbsp;

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:11.760
Teachers could barely hold back the students that&nbsp;
came crowding out, trying to get a better look as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:17.120
the paramedics came to take Elly away. As they&nbsp;
lifted her body onto a stretcher, nobody noticed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:26.240
something fall from her pocket. An unused Knotty&nbsp;
Stalker doll, a brand-new instance of SCP-693.&nbsp;

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:33.440
Now go and check out “SCP-1562 THE&nbsp;
CARNIVOROUS SLIDE” and “SCP-137 A REAL TOY”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:37.680
if you want to know more about anomalies that&nbsp;
might seem like harmless fun and games at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:41.840
but can quickly become the stuff of&nbsp;
childhood nightmares if you aren’t careful!

